Changes include a Debian Slim base, a compressed chromedp headless Chromium bundle,
smaller package selection, bounded journal storage, and revised boot/setup
scripts and service configuration. Shelley is installed separately by exe.dev.

Debian and the packages included in the built image retain their own licenses.
Package copyright information remains under /usr/share/doc in the image.

The browser bundle is supplied by chromedp/docker-headless-shell.
Its build recipe is Copyright (c) 2016-2026 Kenneth Shaw, MIT licensed.
Chromium and its bundled components retain their upstream licenses.
The Chromium BSD license and chromedp MIT license are included under licenses/.

Git is compiled from the Debian source package without source changes, with
size-oriented build options. Git and its components retain their licenses,
including GPL-2.0. The image preserves its copyright and source metadata;
the git-sources build target exports corresponding source archives and recipe.
